Optional: Install Greek and Hebrew Fonts
Installing additional fonts can improve the display of Greek, Hebrew, and other special characters, particularly in terminal output.

There are two options: install fonts through your package manager or download and install them manually.

Fonts: Two options, one use the internet to install, or two, download the fonts and install at your leisure



Option A: Online installation
sudo apt install fonts-dejavu fonts-noto


Option B: Offline font installation

Use this method when you want to download font files manually.

1. Create a directory for the fonts
mkdir -p ~/fonts-offline
cd ~/fonts-offline

2. Download the fonts
mkdir -p ~/fonts-offline && cd ~/fonts-offline

# Cousine: monospace with accented Greek and pointed Hebrew (best terminal font)
curl -LO "https://github.com/google/fonts/raw/main/ofl/cousine/Cousine-Regular.ttf"
curl -LO "https://github.com/google/fonts/raw/main/ofl/cousine/Cousine-Bold.ttf"
curl -LO "https://github.com/google/fonts/raw/main/ofl/cousine/Cousine-Italic.ttf"
curl -LO "https://github.com/google/fonts/raw/main/ofl/cousine/Cousine-BoldItalic.ttf"

# Noto Sans Mono (Greek) and Noto Sans Hebrew (Hebrew fallback)
curl -L -o NotoSansMono.ttf   "https://github.com/google/fonts/raw/main/ofl/notosansmono/NotoSansMono%5Bwdth,wght%5D.ttf"
curl -L -o NotoSansHebrew.ttf "https://github.com/google/fonts/raw/main/ofl/notosanshebrew/NotoSansHebrew%5Bwdth,wght%5D.ttf"
curl -L -o NotoSerif.ttf      "https://github.com/google/fonts/raw/main/ofl/notoserif/NotoSerif%5Bwdth,wght%5D.ttf"

# DejaVu (whole family: Sans, Serif, Mono)
curl -LO "https://github.com/dejavu-fonts/dejavu-fonts/releases/download/version_2_37/dejavu-fonts-ttf-2.37.tar.bz2"

# Gentium Plus (Greek for documents)
curl -LO "https://github.com/silnrsi/font-gentium/releases/download/v6.200/GentiumPlus-6.200.zip"

# Ezra SIL (Hebrew, the font the BDB lexicon was formatted for)
curl -L -o EzraSIL.ttf "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/eliranwong/unabridged-BDB-Hebrew-lexicon/master/sileot.ttf"

ls -lh

3. Install the fonts (or just let them sit there knowing you have them and can install later)
  cd fonts-offline
  tar xjf dejavu-fonts-ttf-2.37.tar.bz2 && unzip -q GentiumPlus-6.200.zip
  mkdir -p ~/.local/share/fonts
  find . -name '*.ttf' -exec cp {} ~/.local/share/fonts/ \;
  fc-cache -f && fc-list | grep -iE 'cousine|noto|dejavu|gentium|ezra' | head
